# Update documentation with code changes

When you **resolve an issue**, **change behavior**, or **add functionality**, update the relevant doc in the same task — not as a follow-up.

## Feature doc map

| Area | Doc to update |
|------|----------------|
| Market page (`src/features/market/**`) | [docs/market-page.md](../../docs/market-page.md) |
| Admin candles pane (`src/features/admin/candles/**`) | [docs/candles-pane.md](../../docs/candles-pane.md) |
| Cursor rules/skills (`.cursor/rules/**`, `.cursor/skills/**`) | [docs/cursor-rules-skills.md](../../docs/cursor-rules-skills.md) |

## What to update

- UI controls, routes, load/error/empty states
- API endpoints, request/response usage, env flags
- Known behavior, prerequisites, and troubleshooting notes
- Source file map when files are added, renamed, or removed

## Cross-cutting changes

Also touch when relevant:

- [docs/aws-urls.md](../../docs/aws-urls.md) — production routes or URLs
- [docs/environment.md](../../docs/environment.md) — new or changed `VITE_*` flags
- [docs/market-page.md](../../docs/market-page.md) — Market page APIs section when endpoints or payloads change
- [docs/README.md](../../docs/README.md) — doc index when adding or removing docs
- [docs/cursor-rules-skills.md](../../docs/cursor-rules-skills.md) — when adding, renaming, or removing project rules/skills

Keep edits focused: document **what changed and why**, avoid duplicating entire contracts in feature docs.
